---
import DetailLayout from "../../layouts/DetailLayout.astro";
---

<DetailLayout
  title="Balagezong Canyon"
  description="Balagezong Canyon, Shangri-La Yunnan: dramatic gorge with hanging coffins, Tibetan villages, and a glass skywalk. Transport, tickets, and travel tips."
  category="Attraction"
  image="balagezong-canyon.webp"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "TouristAttraction",
    "name": "Balagezong Canyon",
    "description": "A dramatic canyon near Shangri-La featuring hanging coffins, traditional Tibetan villages, and a thrilling glass skywalk. Less touristy than Tiger Leaping Gorge but equally impressive.",
    "publicAccess": true
  }}
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Balagezong Canyon</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate-500">A dramatic canyon with hanging coffins, pristine Tibetan villages, and a glass skywalk. Less touristy than Tiger Leaping Gorge but every bit as impressive. An underrated gem.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Altitude</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">2,200&ndash;4,000 m</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Time Needed</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">4&ndash;6 hrs</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Best Season</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">May&ndash;Oct</span></div>
    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-50 p-3 text-center"><span class="block text-xs text-slate-400">Ticket</span><span class="block mt-0.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">170 RMB</span></div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Balagezong (u5df4u62c9u683cu5b97) is a spectacular canyon and scenic area about 80 km from Shangri-La, nestled deep in the Hengduan Mountains where the Yunnan-Tibet-Sichuan borders converge. Unlike the busier Tiger Leaping Gorge, Balagezong remains relatively undiscovered by foreign tourists, offering a raw, immersive experience of Tibetan highland landscapes.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The scenic area encompasses a deep river canyon, several traditional Tibetan villages (including <strong>Bala Village</strong>, a 1,300-year-old settlement), alpine lakes, and a famous <strong>glass skywalk</strong> perched on a vertical cliff face. The canyon walls rise up to 700 meters in places, with the Gangqu River roaring through the narrowest sections. Ancient <strong>hanging coffins</strong> of the Tibetan Naxi people, suspended on canyon walls, add an air of mystery.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">The park is managed with shuttle buses connecting the main sights, making it accessible for all fitness levels. Photography opportunities are exceptional: the contrast of blue sky, red canyon walls, green forest, and white snow peaks in the distance creates compositions that rival anywhere in Yunnan.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">How to Get There</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Balagezong is 80 km from Shangri-La city. The only practical option is a <strong>private car or taxi</strong>, costing <strong>400&ndash;600 RMB</strong> round trip (1.5 hours each way). There is no direct public bus. Most hotels and hostels in Shangri-La can arrange a driver. The road is well-paved but winding through mountain terrain.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">What to See &amp; Do</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Glass Skywalk</h4><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A transparent walkway jutting out from a sheer cliff face, suspended hundreds of meters above the canyon floor. Not for the faint-hearted, but the views and the adrenaline rush are unforgettable.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Bala Village</h4><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A 1,300-year-old Tibetan farming village still inhabited today. Whitewashed houses, barley terraces, and prayer flag-draped hills. The village has a small tea house and basic restaurant.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Hanging Coffins</h4><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Ancient burial coffins suspended on the vertical canyon walls by the Naxi people centuries ago. Visible from the canyon trail. Their purpose and method of placement remain debated.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4"><h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">River Walk &amp; Waterfalls</h4><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600">A wooden walkway follows the Gangqu River through the narrowest section of the canyon, passing seasonal waterfalls and offering close-up views of the rushing rapids.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Food &amp; Dining</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">Bala Village has a basic Tibetan restaurant serving noodle soup (20&ndash;30 RMB), stir-fried dishes, and yak butter tea. The scenic area entrance has a few food stalls with snacks and drinks. For a more substantial meal, wait until you return to Shangri-La. Pack snacks and at least 1.5 liters of water.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Travel Tips</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Wear sturdy shoes &mdash; some trails are uneven and the glass walkway can be slippery after rain.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Morning visits offer the clearest skies. Afternoon clouds often roll into the canyon.</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-emerald-600 font-bold flex-shrink-0">&rarr;</span> <span>Much of the scenic area requires using park shuttle buses. Wait times are reasonable (10&ndash;15 minutes).</span></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-emerald-700">Nearby &raquo;</p>
    <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/attractions/tiger-leaping-gorge" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Tiger Leaping Gorge</a>
      <a href="/attractions/meili-snow-mountain" class="rounded-full bg-white border border-slate-200 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate-700 hover:border-emerald-300 hover:text-emerald-700 transition-colors">Meili Snow Mountain</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</DetailLayout>